# CopilotCAD rules

The full, canonical rule set lives in **`AGENTS.md`** at the repo root. Read it before
making changes. The essentials it covers:

- **Spec-driven:** features are F-0xx in `docs/Docs_001/feature_roadmap_001.md`; each has
  a contract in `specs/specs_001/F-0xx_*.md`. Do not implement until the user approves
  the spec. Do not edit `feature_roadmap_001.md` or `architecture_001.md` unless asked.
- **Architecture boundaries:** OCCT only in `backend/kernel/occt_bridge.py`; the frontend
  never writes project files; the renderer stays sandboxed (`nodeIntegration: false`,
  `contextIsolation: true`); no new JSON-RPC methods unless the spec requires them.
- When implementing F-0xx: read the spec, set `.cursor/feature-scope.json`, then run
  `verify-backend` and/or `verify-frontend`.

Use skill `implement-f-feature` when starting feature implementation. Keep rule changes
in `AGENTS.md` so Cursor and Claude Code never diverge.
